# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Primitives {#primitives}"
msgstr "Mga Primitive {#primitives}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All physical systems, whether classical or quantum, can exist in different states. For example, a car on a road can have a certain mass, position, speed, or acceleration that characterize its state. Similarly, quantum systems can also have different configurations or states, but they differ from classical systems in how we deal with measurements and state evolution. This leads to unique properties such as *superposition* and *entanglement* that are exclusive to quantum mechanics. Just like we can describe a car's state using physical properties like speed or acceleration, we can also describe the state of a quantum system using *observables*, which are mathematical objects.\n"
msgstr "Ang lahat ng pisikal na sistema, maging klasikal man o quantum, ay maaaring umiral sa iba't ibang estado. Halimbawa, ang isang sasakyan sa daan ay maaaring magkaroon ng tiyak na masa, posisyon, bilis, o akselerasyon na nagpapakilala ng kanyang estado. Katulad nito, ang mga quantum na sistema ay maaari ring magkaroon ng iba't ibang konpigurasyon o estado, ngunit naiiba ang mga ito sa mga klasikal na sistema pagdating sa pagsukat at ebolusyon ng estado. Nagbubunga ito ng natatanging katangian tulad ng *superposition* at *entanglement* na eksklusibo sa quantum mechanics. Tulad ng paglalarawan sa estado ng sasakyan gamit ang mga pisikal na katangian tulad ng bilis o akselerasyon, maaari rin nating ilarawan ang estado ng isang quantum na sistema gamit ang mga *observable*, na mga bagay na matematikal.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In quantum mechanics, states are represented by normalized complex column vectors, or *kets* ($|\\psi\\rangle$), and observables are Hermitian linear operators ($\\hat{H}=\\hat{H}^{\\dagger}$) that act on the kets. An eigenvector ($|\\lambda\\rangle$) of an observable is known as an *eigenstate*. Measuring an observable for one of its eigenstates ($|\\lambda\\rangle$) will give us the corresponding eigenvalue ($\\lambda$) as readout.\n"
msgstr "Sa quantum mechanics, ang mga estado ay kinakatawan ng mga normalized na kumplikadong column vector, o mga *ket* ($|\\psi\\rangle$), at ang mga observable ay mga Hermitian linear operator ($\\hat{H}=\\hat{H}^{\\dagger}$) na kumikilos sa mga ket. Ang isang eigenvector ($|\\lambda\\rangle$) ng isang observable ay kilala bilang *eigenstate*. Ang pagsukat ng isang observable para sa isa sa mga eigenstate nito ($|\\lambda\\rangle$) ay magbibigay sa atin ng kaukulang eigenvalue ($\\lambda$) bilang resulta.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you're wondering how to measure a quantum system and what you can measure, Qiskit offers two <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Basic and fundamental operations or data type. Qiskit has the Sampler and Estimator primitives to serve as building blocks to easily construct complex algorithmic workloads.\">primitives</DefinitionTooltip> that can help:\n"
msgstr "Kung nag-iisip ka kung paano sukatin ang isang quantum na sistema at kung ano ang maaaring sukatin, nag-aalok ang Qiskit ng dalawang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Mga pangunahing at pundasyon na operasyon o uri ng datos. Ang Qiskit ay may Sampler at Estimator primitive na nagsisilbing mga bloke ng gusali para madaling bumuo ng mga kumplikadong workload na algoritmiko.\">primitive</DefinitionTooltip> na makakatulong:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`Sampler`: Given a quantum state $|\\psi\\rangle$, this primitive obtains the probability of each possible computational basis state.\n"
msgstr "`Sampler`: Binibigyan ng isang quantum na estado na $|\\psi\\rangle$, kinukuha ng primitive na ito ang posibilidad ng bawat posibleng computational basis state.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`Estimator`: Given a quantum observable $\\hat{H}$ and a state $|\\psi\\rangle$, this primitive computes the expected value of $\\hat{H}$.\n"
msgstr "`Estimator`: Binibigyan ng isang quantum observable na $\\hat{H}$ at isang estado na $|\\psi\\rangle$, kinakalkula ng primitive na ito ang expectation value ng $\\hat{H}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Sampler primitive {#the-sampler-primitive}"
msgstr "Ang Sampler primitive {#the-sampler-primitive}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `Sampler` primitive calculates the probability of obtaining each possible state $|k\\rangle$ from the computational basis, given a quantum circuit that prepares the state $|\\psi\\rangle$. It calculates\n"
msgstr "Ang `Sampler` primitive ay kinakalkula ang posibilidad ng pagkuha ng bawat posibleng estado na $|k\\rangle$ mula sa computational basis, binibigyan ng quantum circuit na naghahanda ng estado na $|\\psi\\rangle$. Kinakalkula nito ang\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p_k = |\\langle k | \\psi \\rangle|^2 \\quad \\forall k \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^n \\equiv \\{0,1,\\cdots,2^n-1\\},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p_k = |\\langle k | \\psi \\rangle|^2 \\quad \\forall k \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^n \\equiv \\{0,1,\\cdots,2^n-1\\},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Where $n$ is the number of qubits, and $k$ the integer representation of any possible output binary string $\\{0,1\\}^n$ (that is, integers base $2$).\n"
msgstr "Kung saan ang $n$ ay ang bilang ng mga qubit, at ang $k$ ang integer na representasyon ng anumang posibleng output binary string na $\\{0,1\\}^n$ (iyon ay, mga integer base $2$).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The IBM Quantum [`Sampler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/sampler-v2) runs the circuit multiple times on a quantum device, performing measurements on each run, and reconstructing the probability distribution from the recovered bitstrings. The more runs (or *shots*) it performs, the more accurate the results will be, but this requires more time and quantum resources.\n"
msgstr "Ang IBM Quantum [`Sampler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/sampler-v2) ay nagpapatakbo ng circuit nang maraming beses sa isang quantum device, nagsasagawa ng mga pagsukat sa bawat takbo, at nagtatayo muli ng probability distribution mula sa mga nakuhang bitstring. Habang mas maraming takbo (o *shot*) ang isinasagawa nito, mas tumpak ang mga resulta, ngunit nangangailangan ito ng mas maraming oras at quantum na mapagkukunan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "However, since the number of possible outputs grows exponentially with the number of qubits $n$ (that is, $2^n$), the number of shots will need to grow exponentially as well in order to capture a _dense_ probability distribution. Therefore, `Sampler` is only efficient for *sparse* probability distributions; where the target state $|\\psi\\rangle$ must be expressible as a linear combination of the computational basis states, with the number of terms growing at most polynomially with the number of qubits:\n"
msgstr "Gayunpaman, dahil ang bilang ng mga posibleng output ay lumalaki nang eksponensyal sa bilang ng mga qubit na $n$ (iyon ay, $2^n$), ang bilang ng mga shot ay kailangang lumaki rin nang eksponensyal upang makuha ang isang _siksik_ na probability distribution. Samakatuwid, ang `Sampler` ay epektibo lamang para sa mga *maluwag* na probability distribution; kung saan ang target na estado na $|\\psi\\rangle$ ay dapat maipahayag bilang isang linear na kombinasyon ng mga computational basis state, na ang bilang ng mga termino ay lumalaki nang hindi hihigit sa polynomial sa bilang ng mga qubit:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum^{\\text{Poly}(n)}_k w_k |k\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum^{\\text{Poly}(n)}_k w_k |k\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `Sampler` can also be configured to retrieve probabilities from a subsection of the circuit, representing a subset of the total possible states.\n"
msgstr "Ang `Sampler` ay maaari ring i-configure upang makuha ang mga posibilidad mula sa isang subseksyon ng circuit, na kumakatawan sa isang subset ng kabuuang posibleng mga estado.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Estimator primitive {#the-estimator-primitive}"
msgstr "Ang Estimator primitive {#the-estimator-primitive}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `Estimator` primitive calculates the expectation value of an observable $\\hat{H}$ for a quantum state $|\\psi\\rangle$; where the observable probabilities can be expressed as $p_\\lambda = |\\langle\\lambda|\\psi\\rangle|^2$, being $|\\lambda\\rangle$ the eigenstates of the observable $\\hat{H}$. The expectation value is then defined as the average of all possible outcomes $\\lambda$ (that is, the eigenvalues of the observable) of a measurement of the state $|\\psi\\rangle$, weighted by the corresponding probabilities:\n"
msgstr "Kinakalkula ng `Estimator` primitive ang expectation value ng isang observable $\\hat{H}$ para sa isang quantum state $|\\psi\\rangle$; kung saan ang mga probabilidad ng observable ay maaaring ipahayag bilang $p_\\lambda = |\\langle\\lambda|\\psi\\rangle|^2$, na ang $|\\lambda\\rangle$ ay ang mga eigenstate ng observable $\\hat{H}$. Ang expectation value ay tinutukoy bilang average ng lahat ng posibleng resulta $\\lambda$ (ibig sabihin, ang mga eigenvalue ng observable) ng isang pagsukat ng estadong $|\\psi\\rangle$, na binibigyang-timbang ng kaukulang mga probabilidad:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi := \\sum_\\lambda p_\\lambda \\lambda = \\langle \\psi | \\hat{H} | \\psi \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi := \\sum_\\lambda p_\\lambda \\lambda = \\langle \\psi | \\hat{H} | \\psi \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "However, calculating the expectation value of an observable is not always possible, as we often don't know its eigenbasis. The IBM Quantum [`Estimator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/estimator-v2) uses a complex algebraic process to estimate the expectation value on a real quantum device by breaking down the observable into a combination of other observables whose eigenbasis we do know.\n"
msgstr "Gayunpaman, ang pagkalkula ng expectation value ng isang observable ay hindi laging posible, dahil kadalasan ay hindi natin alam ang eigenbasis nito. Ang IBM Quantum [`Estimator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/estimator-v2) ay gumagamit ng kumplikadong algebraic na proseso upang tantiyahin ang expectation value sa isang tunay na quantum device sa pamamagitan ng paghahati-hati ng observable sa kombinasyon ng ibang mga observable na alam natin ang eigenbasis.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In simpler terms, `Estimator` breaks down any observable that it doesn't know how to measure into simpler, measurable observables called <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Set of matrices commonly used in quantum computing to represent and manipulate quantum states, consisting of the identity matrix and the three Pauli matrices (X, Y, and Z).\">Pauli operators</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
"Any operator can be expressed as a combination of $4^n$ Pauli operators.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa mas simpleng salita, hinahati-hati ng `Estimator` ang anumang observable na hindi nito alam kung paano sukatin sa mas simple, nasusukat na mga observable na tinatawag na <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Set of matrices commonly used in quantum computing to represent and manipulate quantum states, consisting of the identity matrix and the three Pauli matrices (X, Y, and Z).\">Pauli operators</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
"Anumang operator ay maaaring ipahayag bilang kombinasyon ng $4^n$ Pauli operators.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{P}_k :=\n"
"\\sigma_{k_{n-1}}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes \\sigma_{k_0} \\quad\n"
"\\forall k \\in \\mathbb{Z}_4^n \\equiv \\{0,1,\\cdots,4^n-1\\}, \\\\\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{P}_k :=\n"
"\\sigma_{k_{n-1}}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes \\sigma_{k_0} \\quad\n"
"\\forall k \\in \\mathbb{Z}_4^n \\equiv \\{0,1,\\cdots,4^n-1\\}, \\\\\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "such that\n"
msgstr "gayong\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H} = \\sum^{4^n-1}_{k=0} w_k \\hat{P}_k\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H} = \\sum^{4^n-1}_{k=0} w_k \\hat{P}_k\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $n$ is the number of qubits, $k \\equiv k_{n-1} \\cdots k_0$ for $k_l \\in \\mathbb{Z}_4 \\equiv \\{0, 1, 2, 3\\}$ (that is, integers base $4$), and $(\\sigma_0, \\sigma_1, \\sigma_2, \\sigma_3) := (I, X, Y, Z)$.\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $n$ ay ang bilang ng mga qubit, $k \\equiv k_{n-1} \\cdots k_0$ para sa $k_l \\in \\mathbb{Z}_4 \\equiv \\{0, 1, 2, 3\\}$ (ibig sabihin, mga integer base $4$), at $(\\sigma_0, \\sigma_1, \\sigma_2, \\sigma_3) := (I, X, Y, Z)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After performing this decomposition, `Estimator` derives a new circuit $V_k|\\psi\\rangle$ for each observable $\\hat{P}_k$ (from the original circuit), to effectively *diagonalize* the Pauli observable in the computational basis and measure it. We can easily measure Pauli observables because we know $V_k$ ahead of time, which is not the case generally for other observables.\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos isagawa ang decomposition na ito, kinukuha ng `Estimator` ang isang bagong circuit $V_k|\\psi\\rangle$ para sa bawat observable $\\hat{P}_k$ (mula sa orihinal na circuit), upang epektibong *i-diagonalize* ang Pauli observable sa computational basis at sukatin ito. Madali nating masusukat ang mga Pauli observable dahil alam na natin ang $V_k$ nang maaga, na hindi karaniwang totoo para sa ibang mga observable.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each $\\hat{P}_{k}$, the `Estimator` runs the corresponding circuit on a quantum device multiple times, measures the output state in the computational basis, and calculates the probability $p_{kj}$ of obtaining each possible output $j$. It then looks for the eigenvalue $\\lambda_{kj}$ of $P_k$ corresponding to each output $j$, multiplies by $w_k$, and adds all the results together to obtain the expected value of the observable $\\hat{H}$ for the given state $|\\psi\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Para sa bawat $\\hat{P}_{k}$, pinapatakbo ng `Estimator` ang kaukulang circuit sa isang quantum device nang maraming beses, sinusukat ang output state sa computational basis, at kinakalkula ang probabilidad na $p_{kj}$ ng pagkuha ng bawat posibleng output na $j$. Pagkatapos ay hinahanap nito ang eigenvalue na $\\lambda_{kj}$ ng $P_k$ na kaukulan sa bawat output $j$, pinaparami ng $w_k$, at idinaragdag ang lahat ng resulta upang makuha ang expected value ng observable $\\hat{H}$ para sa ibinigay na estadong $|\\psi\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi =\n"
"\\sum_{k=0}^{4^n-1} w_k \\sum_{j=0}^{2^n-1}p_{kj} \\lambda_{kj},\n"
"$$\n"
"Since calculating the expectation value of $4^n$ Paulis is impractical (that is, exponentially growing), `Estimator` can only be efficient when a large amount of $w_k$ are zero (that is, *sparse* Pauli decomposition instead of *dense*). Formally we say that, for this computation to be *efficiently solvable*, the number of non-zero terms has to grow at most polynomially with the number of qubits $n$: $\\hat{H} = \\sum^{\\text{Poly}(n)}_k w_k \\hat{P}_k$.\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi =\n"
"\\sum_{k=0}^{4^n-1} w_k \\sum_{j=0}^{2^n-1}p_{kj} \\lambda_{kj},\n"
"$$\n"
"Dahil hindi praktikal ang pagkalkula ng expectation value ng $4^n$ Paulis (ibig sabihin, tumataas nang exponential), ang `Estimator` ay maaari lamang maging episyente kapag ang malaking bilang ng $w_k$ ay zero (ibig sabihin, *sparse* na Pauli decomposition sa halip na *dense*). Pormal nating sasabihin na, upang ang computation na ito ay maging *episyenteng malulutas*, ang bilang ng mga non-zero na termino ay dapat tumaas nang polynomial lamang kasama ng bilang ng mga qubit na $n$: $\\hat{H} = \\sum^{\\text{Poly}(n)}_k w_k \\hat{P}_k$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The reader may notice the implicit assumption that probability <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The process of taking several measurements of one or several things.\">sampling</DefinitionTooltip> also needs to be efficient as explained for `Sampler`, which means\n"
msgstr "Maaaring mapansin ng mambabasa ang implicit na palagay na ang posibilidad na <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Ang proseso ng pagsasagawa ng ilang pagsukat ng isa o ilang mga bagay.\">sampling</DefinitionTooltip> ay kailangan ding maging mahusay tulad ng ipinaliwanag para sa `Sampler`, na ibig sabihin ay\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi =\n"
"\\sum_{k}^{\\text{Poly}(n)} w_k \\sum_{j}^{\\text{Poly}(n)}p_{kj} \\lambda_{kj}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi =\n"
"\\sum_{k}^{\\text{Poly}(n)} w_k \\sum_{j}^{\\text{Poly}(n)}p_{kj} \\lambda_{kj}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Guided example to calculate expectation values {#guided-example-to-calculate-expectation-values}"
msgstr "Patnubay na halimbawa para sa pagkalkula ng mga expectation value {#guided-example-to-calculate-expectation-values}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's assume the single-qubit state $|+\\rangle := H|0\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle)$, and observable\n"
msgstr "Ipagpalagay nating ang single-qubit state na $|+\\rangle := H|0\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle)$, at observable\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\hat{H}\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"-1 & 2 \\\\\n"
"2 & 1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = 2X - Z\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\hat{H}\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"-1 & 2 \\\\\n"
"2 & 1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = 2X - Z\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with the following theoretical expectation value $\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_+ = \\langle+|\\hat{H}|+\\rangle = 2$.\n"
msgstr "na may sumusunod na teoretikal na expectation value na $\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_+ = \\langle+|\\hat{H}|+\\rangle = 2$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since we do not know how to measure this observable, we cannot compute its expectation value directly, and we need to re-express it as $\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_+ = 2\\langle X \\rangle_+ - \\langle Z \\rangle_+ $. Which can be shown to evaluate to the same result by virtue of noting that $\\langle+|X|+\\rangle = 1$, and $\\langle+|Z|+\\rangle = 0$.\n"
msgstr "Dahil hindi natin alam kung paano sukatin ang observable na ito, hindi natin direktang makalkula ang expectation value nito, at kailangan nating muling ipahayag ito bilang $\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_+ = 2\\langle X \\rangle_+ - \\langle Z \\rangle_+ $. Maaaring ipakita na ito ay nagbibigay ng parehong resulta sa pamamagitan ng pagpansin na $\\langle+|X|+\\rangle = 1$, at $\\langle+|Z|+\\rangle = 0$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let see how to compute $\\langle X \\rangle_+$ and $\\langle Z \\rangle_+$ directly. Since $X$ and $Z$ do not commute (that is, they don't share the same eigenbasis), they cannot be measured simultaneously, therefore we need the auxiliary circuits:\n"
msgstr "Tingnan natin kung paano direktang kalkulahin ang $\\langle X \\rangle_+$ at $\\langle Z \\rangle_+$. Dahil ang $X$ at $Z$ ay hindi nagkokomyut (iyon ay, hindi sila nagbabahagi ng parehong eigenbasis), hindi sila maaaring sukatin nang sabay-sabay, kaya kailangan natin ang mga auxiliary circuit:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/cost-functions/extracted-outputs/7c32e970-f9cb-48ec-a60b-2dccb0744141-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/cost-functions/extracted-outputs/7c32e970-f9cb-48ec-a60b-2dccb0744141-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/cost-functions/extracted-outputs/ec3cf7af-66b2-4ea9-94d7-6ec6ba2bfc5e-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/cost-functions/extracted-outputs/ec3cf7af-66b2-4ea9-94d7-6ec6ba2bfc5e-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
